.TH XD\-MINES 1 2026-10-22 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-mines \- Minefield
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-mines
.OP \-\-seed N
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-mines
is Minefield, Windows XP's mine-clearing game, drawn as XP drew it
whatever the theme.
Left click opens a square: a number says how many mines touch it, and a
square with none opens the empty area around it.
Right click flags a square, then (with Game > Marks) marks it with a
question mark.
Both buttons, or the middle one, on a number whose flags are all placed
open its other neighbours.
The first square opened is never a mine.
Opening every square without a mine wins; the face button (or F2) starts
a new game.
.PP
Game > Beginner (9 by 9, 10 mines), Intermediate (16 by 16, 40), Expert
(30 by 16, 99) or Custom (up to 30 by 24), and Best Times, the fastest
win at each level.
They're kept in
.IR ~/.config/xeondesktop/mines.ini .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-seed N
Lay the mines from seed
.I N
(the same each time), for tests.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-shell (1)
